    "statement": "Retain an official Shape-A all-excess survivor and any minimal tensor presentation G(t,X)=sum_(j=0)^(r-1) A_j(t)B_j(X) with r>=2. The parameter coefficient map a:P^1->P^(r-1) is basepoint-free. If d is its degree onto the image, then d divides m=e-2. The exact Shape-A column deficit sum_delta(a_delta+r_delta)=2e-7 permits at most one slope of Gamma to have no actual U_0 incidence. Every active slope lies in a complete reduced degree-d fiber of the normalization map, because an incident exact split row pulls back a hyperplane section with only simple roots in Gamma. Hence d divides either 3e or 3e-1. On the official row gcd(m,3e)=gcd(m,6)=1 and gcd(m,3e-1)=gcd(m,5)=1, so d=1. Thus the parameter coefficient map in every nontrivial minimal tensor presentation is birational onto its projective image.",
